# Valgrind suppressions for misha's forked multitasking workers.
#
# R-hub's valgrind platform appends this file to the container's default.supp
# (r-hub/actions/run-check/scripts/valgrind-suppressions.sh) and then fails the job for any
# non-zero "ERROR SUMMARY", so without it the platform is permanently red and its output stops
# being read.
#
# What it covers. A misha multitasking child ends through rexit(), which raises SIGTERM on
# itself so the process dies WITHOUT unwinding - see rule C4 of the lifetime contract at the top
# of src/rdbutils.h. That is deliberate: a child that unwound into R's error path would run R's
# shutdown, including the part that removes the session temp directory it does not own. The cost
# is that whatever R and its dependencies allocated during their own start-up is still held when
# valgrind takes its snapshot, and three of those blocks are reachable only through interior
# pointers, so memcheck files them as "possibly lost".
#
# Measured on the R-hub valgrind run of 2026-08-23 (misha 5.11.21, run 32639267717): 30 forked
# children, each reporting exactly these three allocation shapes and nothing else - 5 contexts,
# 962 bytes, zero definitely lost, zero errors of any other kind. Every one of them is allocated
# by R, glibc or OpenBLAS during start-up; not one has a misha frame in it. Reproduced locally
# under valgrind 3.27.1 against a two-kid gextract, with the same three stacks in the kids and
# none of them in the parent.
#
# What it deliberately does NOT cover. Each entry pins "possibly lost" only, and pins the
# allocating function, so a block misha itself leaks - or anything lost definitely or
# indirectly - is still reported. If a new context appears here, that is a finding: read it
# before adding to this file.

{
   misha-multitasking-child-exit-R-setenv-string
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: possible
   fun:malloc
   fun:__add_to_environ
   fun:setenv
}

{
   misha-multitasking-child-exit-glibc-environ-tsearch-node
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: possible
   fun:malloc
   fun:tsearch
   fun:__add_to_environ
   fun:setenv
}

{
   misha-multitasking-child-exit-openblas-thread-tls
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: possible
   fun:calloc
   ...
   fun:_dl_allocate_tls
   ...
   fun:blas_thread_init
}
